[h1]🇺🇦 Barony Ukrainian Localization[/h1]
[i]Game version: v5.0.2 · localization release: 5.0.2-2[/i]

Ukrainian localization of Barony: the interface, items, monsters, spells, compendium, achievements, story texts and seasonal themes. The original game files are not modified — the mod can be turned off at any time.

[b]Status:[/b] this is the first, [b]unproofread[/b] version. The texts are in Ukrainian but have not been reviewed by an editor yet — expect occasional inaccuracies, awkward wording or lines that run long. Proofreading is in progress; updates will follow as they are ready.

[h2]How to enable[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe to the mod.
[*]Launch Barony: main menu → [b]Custom Content[/b] → [b]Workshop Mods[/b] → «Українська локалізація Barony» → [b]Load Mod[/b].
[*]Restart the game if asked.
[/olist]

[h2]Alternative installation[/h2]
The mod files can be copied straight into the game folder — Ukrainian is then on from the start, without picking the mod in the menu.

[olist]
[*]Subscribe to the mod and wait until Steam downloads it.
[*]Open the mod folder. With a default Steam install it is:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\workshop\content\371970\3711160804[/code]
If Steam or the game is elsewhere: in your Steam library right-click Barony → [b]Manage → Browse local files[/b] — that opens the game folder; the mod folder is next to it, in [code]...\steamapps\workshop\content\371970\3711160804[/code].
[*]Copy [b]everything[/b] from the mod folder (the [code]lang[/code], [code]data[/code], [code]items[/code], [code]books[/code], [code]fonts[/code], [code]themes[/code] folders) into the game folder — by default:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Barony[/code]
and confirm replacing the files.
[/olist]

[i]Back up the game folder first: verifying the game files in Steam restores the originals and undoes the changes.[/i]

Without the Workshop: download the archive from GitHub (Releases) and unpack it so that you get the folder
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Barony\mods\Barony Ukrainian Localization[/code]
(i.e. inside [code]mods[/code] there is a [code]Barony Ukrainian Localization[/code] folder with the mod files). Then in the game: [b]Custom Content → Local Mods → Barony Ukrainian Localization → Load Mod[/b].

[h2]What is translated[/h2]
[list]
[*]Interface: menus, settings, tooltips, in-game messages
[*]Items, spells, monsters, classes and races, achievements
[*]Compendium (all entries)
[*]Story texts, the tutorial and all 34 books
[*]Seasonal themes
[*]Not translated: text baked into maps or the game code
[/list]

[h2]Known issues[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Not proofread yet.[/b] All texts are in Ukrainian, but an editor has not reviewed them — expect occasional inaccuracies, awkward wording and typos. Proofreading is in progress.
[*][b]Long lines.[/b] Some labels may not fit narrow buttons, tables or tooltips.
[*][b]Garbled characters.[/b] In some places broken symbols appear instead of letters. Being worked on, will be fixed in upcoming releases.
[*][b]Fonts.[/b] Some letters are drawn incorrectly and are hard to recognize. Will be fixed in upcoming releases.
[*][b]Labels from the game code.[/b] A few abbreviations are hard-coded in the game and stay in Latin (e.g. «LVL» above the XP bar). May be resolved with a new version of the game.
[*][b]Books after disabling the mod.[/b] The game compiles the books into
[code]books\compiled_books.json[/code]
in its own folder and does not always restore the original after the mod is disabled — the books then stay in Ukrainian or the game complains on start. If that happens, delete the file or verify the game files in Steam. Likely to be resolved with a new version of the game.
[/list]

[h2]Bugs and suggestions[/h2]
Found a mistake, an untranslated line or text overflowing its frame — leave a comment or open an issue on GitHub:

[url=https://github.com/UKA-Localization/Barony-localization-uk-UA]Barony-localization-uk-UA — GitHub[/url]

No technical skills are needed to help with proofreading: just read the texts and flag what sounds unnatural in Ukrainian.

